{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"C3: Challenge: the search with one more connective","title_html":"C3: Challenge: the search with one more connective","html":"<p>Extend search trees by the rules of C1 for <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbin{|}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"BIN\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. Prove that <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"prp-search-decides\">@prp-search-decides</span> still holds\nfor lists of formulas of the extended language: give the new cases of\neach part of its proof.</p>","file":"ch4/refuting-row-search.html"}